^["open"]{
 ?[half_spaced_dot]: "Should `a. b` and `a .b` be diagnostics in the first AssociationIR capability, or carry prefix/postfix dot meanings from day one? Decides whether ~[association_semantics] can ship without operator-dot semantics."
 # resolved: [qualified_token] — keep IDENTIFIER plus segment metadata; see stream 2026-08-24 11:47
 # moved: [bundle_entrypoints] — public entry points are owned by ~"../package-iteration-radius/wip.spw" ?[entrypoint_matrix]; see stream 2026-08-24 12:58
 ?[newline_scope]: "Which dialects treat cadence (one line break) and episode (blank line) as semantically different, and which project both to open? Decides the per-dialect table AssociationIR needs in ~[association_semantics]."
 ?[product_boundary]: "Is the `index` depth a parser product or a workspace-owned derivation over structure products? Decides whether progressive-product/1 advertises an index stage."
 ?[policy_surface]: "May a file carry a local format override that cannot change semantic affinity, given the decision for one workspace policy with deterministic layers? Decides the layering in ~[association_spacing_format]."
 ?[spread_resolution]: "Should signal resolution stay hidden behind --spread until benchmarks exist, or become its own declared profile? Decides whether the coupled minimal|standard|full index presets are split."
 ?[alias_retirement_boundary]: "Which release removes --product, --event-policy, --limit, and the --depth corpus form together? Decides the alias retirement notice date."
 ?[block_cache_identity]: "Which normalized block identity survives nearby edits yet stays cheap enough for editor-local warming? Decides the key shape for block-level cache reuse."
 ?[notation_exhibit]: "Should a notation node preserve lexed tokens and dialect identity while withholding runtime interpretation? Carried from the closed spw-syntax-warning-cleanup plan, whose file-level exhibit separation did not add a node."
 ?[relation_vocabulary]: "Which typed relation nodes, if any, should own recurring >, =>, and == surfaces? Decides whether AssociationIR needs a relation kind."
 ?[signed_numeric]: "Under which gap and fixity rules does a leading sign belong to the number instead of being an operator? Decides the numeric case in ~[association_semantics]."
 ?[collection_choice]: "Which migration keeps legacy lists, explicit #[...] collections, and `a | b | c` choice from becoming silently equivalent? Decides whether formatter proposals for collections can be typed."
 ?[probe_order]: "Should the PLAN.md corpus probe naming scripts/analyzers/spw-gap-census.ts be marked as running only after ~[gap_census_bench] creates that [NEW] file? Tracked at ~"../lukewarm-backlog/wip.spw" ?[gap_probe_order]."
}

