#>wonder_gap_affinity_tooling_1
?["When does a space become language rather than layout?"]{
  ~#answer_shape: [#declared_profile, #gap_class, #association_delta, #counterexample]
  ~#baseline: "spw inspect spacing --text on a.b, a. b, a .b, a . b: gaps 0, 2, 2, 2; qualifiedIdentifiers 1, 0, 0, 0; all four parse with 0 errors under Spw.b, so half-spaced dots are silently accepted today"
  !probe{ "remove or insert one gap, compare AssociationIR, and refuse a layout-only label when the semantic hash changes. Until ~[association_semantics] lands there is no AssociationIR, so rerun the baseline: npm run -s spw -- inspect spacing --text 'a. b' --json and check whether the diagnostics change." }
  $%[gap.class, association.hash, differential.stratum]
}

#>wonder_gap_affinity_tooling_2
?["How little parsing can answer this question truthfully?"]{
  ~#answer_shape: [#requested_product, #completeness, #elapsed, #omitted]
  !probe{ "run the same question through tokens, structure, semantic, and trace requests; the first complete product is the useful cost floor." }
  $%[product.stage, product.elapsed_ms, event.count]
}
